{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeyRecorder(options): VueHotkeyRecorder;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeyRecorder.ts#L62","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeyRecorder.ts:62"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue composable for recording keyboard shortcuts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This composable provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":"\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration options for the recorder"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/VueHotkeyRecorder.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueHotkeyRecorder"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object with recording state and control functions"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeyRecorder } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst shortcut = ref<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\nconst recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n  onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n    shortcut.value = hotkey\n  },\n  onCancel: () => {\n    console.log('Recording cancelled')\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <button @click=\"recorder.startRecording()\">\n      {{ recorder.isRecording ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut' }}\n    </button>\n    <div v-if=\"recorder.recordedHotkey\">\n      Recording: {{ recorder.recordedHotkey }}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeyRecorder(options): VueHotkeyRecorder;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeyRecorder.ts:62](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeyRecorder.ts#L62)\n\nVue composable for recording keyboard shortcuts.\n\nThis composable provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic `HotkeyRecorder`\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`HotkeyRecorderOptions`\\>\n\nConfiguration options for the recorder\n\n## Returns\n\n[`VueHotkeyRecorder`](../interfaces/VueHotkeyRecorder.md)\n\nAn object with recording state and control functions\n\n## Example\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeyRecorder } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst shortcut = ref<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\nconst recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n  onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n    shortcut.value = hotkey\n  },\n  onCancel: () => {\n    console.log('Recording cancelled')\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <button @click=\"recorder.startRecording()\">\n      {{ recorder.isRecording ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut' }}\n    </button>\n    <div v-if=\"recorder.recordedHotkey\">\n      Recording: {{ recorder.recordedHotkey }}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeyRecorder\ntitle: useHotkeyRecorder\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeyRecorder(options): VueHotkeyRecorder;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeyRecorder.ts:62](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeyRecorder.ts#L62)\n\nVue composable for recording keyboard shortcuts.\n\nThis composable provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic `HotkeyRecorder`\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`HotkeyRecorderOptions`\\>\n\nConfiguration options for the recorder\n\n## Returns\n\n[`VueHotkeyRecorder`](../interfaces/VueHotkeyRecorder.md)\n\nAn object with recording state and control functions\n\n## Example\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeyRecorder } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst shortcut = ref<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\nconst recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n  onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n    shortcut.value = hotkey\n  },\n  onCancel: () => {\n    console.log('Recording cancelled')\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <button @click=\"recorder.startRecording()\">\n      {{ recorder.isRecording ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut' }}\n    </button>\n    <div v-if=\"recorder.recordedHotkey\">\n      Recording: {{ recorder.recordedHotkey }}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n"}
